      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/0369816d7be767d43d19d9d4f337058ec732bc185ce9a385347997068a4f0404.png)\n\nWhat inequality describes the shaded region shown above?\n\n$y$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "We need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is dashed, we will use a strict inequality. Since the shaded region is *above* the line, the inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line.\n\nSo, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>3x-1.\n$$",
